==Teams==
A total of 18 teams are contesting the league, including 11 sides from the [[2022–23 Saudi First Division League|2022–23 season]], the five promoted teams from the [[2022–23 Saudi Second Division|Second Division]] and the two relegated sides from the [[2022–23 Saudi Professional League|Pro League]].

[[Al Batin FC|Al-Batin]] were the first club to be relegated following a 1–0 defeat away to [[Al-Ittihad Club (Jeddah)|Al-Ittihad]] on 23 May 2023.<ref>{{cite web |title=الباطن.. 2023.. الحصيلة الأسوأ |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/806694/}}</ref> Al-Batin were relegated after three years in the top flight. [[Al-Adalah FC|Al-Adalah]] were the second and final club to be relegated following a 2–0 home defeat to [[Ettifaq FC|Al-Ettifaq]] on the final matchday.<ref>{{cite web |title=بعد 367 يوما.. العدالة يعود إلى "يلو" |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/807521/}}</ref> Al-Adalah were relegated after just one year in the top flight. Both Al-Adalah and Al-Batin will play in their 7th season in the FD League.

The first club to be promoted was [[Al-Najma SC (Saudi Arabia)|Al-Najma]] who did so after a 1–1 draw against [[Al-Kawkab FC|Al-Kawkab]] on 17 March 2023.<ref>{{cite web |title=بعد عشر سنوات فريق النجمة يعود لدوري يلو |url=https://www.alriyadh.com/2003162}}</ref> On 24 March 2023, [[Al-Taraji Club|Al-Taraji]] became the second club to be promoted despite a 1–0 defeat to [[Al-Bukiryah FC|Al-Bukiryah]].<ref>{{cite web |title=لأول مرة في تاريخه... الترجي يصعد إلى "الأولى" |url=https://www.okaz.com.sa/sport/saudi/2129690}}</ref> On 31 March 2023, [[Al-Bukiryah FC|Al-Bukiryah]] became the third club to be promoted following a 1–0 home win against [[Al-Diriyah Club|Al-Diriyah]].<ref>{{cite web |title=البكيرية يعود من جديد إلى دوري يلو لأندية الأولى |url=https://www.al-jazirah.com/2023/20230402/sp6.htm}}</ref> On 8 April 2023, [[Al Safa FC|Al-Safa]] became the fourth club to be promoted following a 2–1 home win against [[Wej SC|Wej]].<ref>{{cite web |title=الصفا يعود لدوري يلو بعد غياب 8 أعوام |url=https://www.alyaum.com/article/6462099}}</ref> The fifth and final club to be promoted was [[Al-Jandal Club|Al-Jandal]], who did so following a 4–2 aggregate win over [[Bisha FC|Bisha]] in the promotion play-offs.<ref>{{cite web |title=الجندل.. صعود تاريخي |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/804131}}</ref>

Al-Najma were crowned champions after defeating Al-Taraji 2–1 to win their third title and first since 2010.<ref>{{cite web |title=رسميًا.. النجمة بطلًا لدوري الدرجة الثانية السعودي |url=https://www.alyaum.com/article/6465145}}</ref>

Al-Najma return to the [[Saudi First Division League|First Division League]] after an absence of 10 years. They return to the league for the first time since the 2012–13 season and will play in their 11th overall season. Al-Bukiryah return after an absence of two seasons and will play in their 3rd overall season in the First Division League. Al-Safa return after an absence of eight years and will play in their 2nd overall season in the First Division League. Both Al-Taraji and Al-Jandal were promoted to the First Division League for the first time in history.

